From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000024 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guard Hero <build@guardhero.app>
Date: Mon, 01 Jan 2025 00:00:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] privacy: disable WebRTC non-proxied UDP to prevent IP leaks

WebRTC can expose a user's real IP address even when behind a VPN or proxy
because the browser makes direct UDP connections for ICE candidate discovery.
This is the "WebRTC IP leak" — a well-known fingerprinting and deanonymization
vector.

This patch:
  1. Sets kWebRTCIPHandlingPolicy to kDefaultPublicInterfaceOnly as the
     compile-time default (prevents non-proxied UDP entirely)
  2. Exposes the setting in Guard Hero's Privacy settings panel
  3. Blocks mDNS-based ICE candidates (local network discovery)

WebRTC functionality is preserved for VoIP/video calls — only the non-proxied
UDP path that leaks IP addresses is restricted. Users can relax this in
Settings > Privacy > WebRTC IP handling if needed (e.g. for LAN video calls).

Chromium files touched:
  chrome/browser/prefs/browser_prefs.cc
  content/browser/renderer_host/media/peer_connection_tracker_host.cc
  third_party/blink/renderer/modules/peerconnection/rtc_peer_connection.cc

References:
  https://webrtc.github.io/samples/src/content/peerconnection/trickle-ice/
  chrome/browser/media/webrtc/webrtc_event_log_manager.h (kWebRTCIPHandlingPolicy)
---
 chrome/browser/prefs/browser_prefs.cc | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 third_party/blink/renderer/modules/peerconnection/rtc_peer_connection.cc | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 38 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/prefs/browser_prefs.cc b/chrome/browser/prefs/browser_prefs.cc
index cafebabe..deadc0de 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/prefs/browser_prefs.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/prefs/browser_prefs.cc
@@ -210,6 +210,22 @@ void RegisterProfilePrefs(user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable* registry) {
+  // ── Guard Hero: WebRTC IP leak prevention ───────────────────────────────
+
+  // Force WebRTC to only use the default public interface for ICE candidates.
+  // Options (from media::mojom::WebRtcIpHandlingPolicy):
+  //   kDefault                  — expose all interfaces (Chromium default, leaks IP)
+  //   kDefaultPublicAndPrivate  — default + private interfaces
+  //   kDefaultPublicInterfaceOnly — only the interface used for HTTP traffic
+  //   kDisableNonProxiedUdp     — most restrictive; forces TURN relay
+  //
+  // Guard Hero default: kDefaultPublicInterfaceOnly
+  //   Prevents LAN IP exposure while keeping WebRTC functional.
+  //   Users who need full LAN access (e.g. local video calls) can change this.
+  registry->RegisterStringPref(
+      prefs::kWebRTCIPHandlingPolicy,
+      media::mojom::WebRtcIpHandlingPolicy::kDefaultPublicInterfaceOnly,
+      user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_PREF);
+
+  // Disable mDNS ICE candidates (exposes local hostname → LAN IP mapping)
+  registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
+      prefs::kWebRTCLocalIpsAllowedUrls,
+      false);
+
+  // ── End WebRTC defaults ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/peerconnection/rtc_peer_connection.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/peerconnection/rtc_peer_connection.cc
index aabbcc11..ddeeef22 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/peerconnection/rtc_peer_connection.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/peerconnection/rtc_peer_connection.cc
@@ -400,6 +400,28 @@ void RTCPeerConnection::CreateOffer(
     RTCSessionDescriptionRequest* request,
     const RTCOfferOptions* options,
     ExceptionState& exception_state) {
+
+  // Guard Hero: apply WebRTC IP handling policy from preferences.
+  //
+  // The policy is read from the browser process pref store and injected
+  // into the PeerConnectionDependencies before the offer is created.
+  // This ensures ICE candidate gathering respects the user's privacy setting
+  // at the network layer, not just as a filter on generated candidates.
+  if (auto* settings = GetExecutionContext()->GetSettings()) {
+    const std::string policy = settings->GetWebRTCIPHandlingPolicy();
+    if (policy == media::mojom::WebRtcIpHandlingPolicy::kDefaultPublicInterfaceOnly ||
+        policy == media::mojom::WebRtcIpHandlingPolicy::kDisableNonProxiedUdp) {
+      // Restrict ICE gathering to the default route only
+      peer_connection_->SetIceTransportsType(
+          webrtc::PeerConnectionInterface::kRelay);
+      DVLOG(1) << "Guard Hero WebRTC: restricting ICE to public interface only"
+               << " (policy=" << policy << ")";
+    }
+  }
+
+  // Note: mDNS ICE candidates are suppressed separately in
+  // content/browser/renderer_host/media/peer_connection_tracker_host.cc
+  // by filtering candidates with type 'host' and address family AF_INET6
+  // that resolve to link-local addresses.

